    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nI'm trying to port some Cython code into pure Python by following [this section of the documentation](https://cython.readthedocs.io/en/latest/src/userguide/language_basics.html#python-objects-as-parameters-and-return-values). It provides me the example code:\n\n```python\nfrom cython.cimports.cpython.ref import PyObject, _Py_REFCNT, Py_REFCNT\n```\n\nThis does not run in Python with Cython installed from the master branch. It gives an `AttributeError` instead.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```python\nfrom cython.cimports.cpython.ref import PyObject, _Py_REFCNT, Py_REFCNT\n```\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n`PyObject`, `_Py_REFCNT`, and `Py_REFCNT` should all be available, either in the REPL or in pure Python code\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.6\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0a2\n\n### Additional context\n\nThe error produced:\n```python\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<python-input-1>\", line 1, in <module>\n    from cython.cimports.cpython.ref import PyObject, _Py_REFCNT, Py_REFCNT\n  File \"<frozen importlib._bootstrap>\", line 1371, in _find_and_load\n  File \"<frozen importlib._bootstrap>\", line 1325, in _find_and_load_unlocked\n  File \"/home/sanotehu/src/cython/Cython/Shadow.py\", line 840, in __getattr__\n    raise AttributeError(item)\nAttributeError: __spec__. Did you mean: '__doc__'?\n```",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-17T19:59:09Z",
