            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This may be a failure of documentation to properly explain pure-Python mode.\n\nNot all pure-Python mode code can realistically run in Python, especially code that uses C functions (like this does). There's definitely a large subset that can, it generally isn't something we can ensure. It's more about using Python-compatible syntax.\n\nIf you want something that's genuinely runable in Python then you'd need to do\n\n```\nimport cython\nif cython.compiled:\n    from cython.cimports.cpython.ref import PyObject, _Py_REFCNT, Py_REFCNT\n```\n\nAlthough obviously the bit that uses all these functions would also need to be guarded by `if cython.compiled`. I imagine `PyObject` is going into type annotations so `from __future__ import annotations` would be an easy way to guard those.",
